body:
@IanVS Just happy to help! :+1:

This is one of the advantages of the `standard` test suite running against [real user code](https://github.com/feross/standard/blob/master/test/clone.js#L3-L9). Currently we test the top ~400 packages that use `standard`, ranked based on the # of npm dependents. You find lots of odd code out there in the wild!

It's a mixed blessing though, as your tests will fail whenever there are lint errors _in other people's code!_ So the [list of repos to test](https://github.com/feross/standard-packages/blob/master/test.json) requires a bit of curation. :)
